From cd0eda512f28e171819e1c852c21a43dac5bbaf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Schindelin <johannes.schindelin@gmx.de>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:45:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/N] Restore DOS text handling for MSYS2

MSYS2 build tooling relies on CR removal from native Windows tool output,
behavior that GNU grep lost on purpose in their upstream commit
https://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/grep.git/commit/?id=5ac3d87a (Simplify
-U on MS-Windows by removing guesswork, 2017-02-14).

Restore that compatibility while retaining -U as the raw-input escape hatch.

Note: Using O_TEXT instead would not be equivalent: it lacks the initial
NUL-based binary classification, preserves embedded lone CRs, and makes -b
count normalized rather than original bytes even without -u. Correct raw-byte
accounting is also necessary for -m resumption on seekable stdin, including
when CR runs cross buffer boundaries.

Assisted-by: GPT-6
Signed-off-by: Johannes Schindelin <johannes.schindelin@gmx.de>
---
 src/Makefile.am |   2 +-
 src/dosbuf.c    | 233 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/grep.c      |  59 ++++++++----
 3 files changed, 278 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/dosbuf.c

